/-
Occurrences of circles in the Descartes quadruples of the packing, and the
combinatorial "circle graph" on them.

An *occurrence* is a pair (quadruple w, index i): the circle that sits at
coordinate i of the Descartes quadruple w.  A circle of the packing appears in
many Descartes quadruples; two occurrences (w, i) and (w', i') are the same
circle when they can be identified along the packing, i.e. when one is
obtained from the other by S-moves that never touch the circle's own
coordinate: (w, j) is the same circle as (gen i • w, j) for every j ≠ i.

Two occurrences are *tangent* when they co-occur in a common Descartes
quadruple at different coordinates.  The *connection* relation combines
tangency and same-circle steps; it is the tangency graph of the packing on
occurrences, and it is connected (every occurrence is connected to the root
quadruple (-3,5,8,8)).  This is the combinatorial skeleton on which the
coprime-path (copath) refinement and the constancy of χ₂ will be built.
-/
import Submission.Apollo.Crack
import Submission.Apollo.Relabel
import Submission.Apollo.Parity
